course: dictionary
lesson: 6480
title: Nautical: words from the sea
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Nautical means to do with ships, sailing and sailors. When you meet it, think of boats, the ocean and the crew. The word can also describe things that look like they belong on a ship.
explain: «Countries also have borders at sea, with territorial waters reaching 12 nautical miles from the coast.» The clues are borders at sea and from the coast. So a nautical mile is a way of measuring distance on the sea, not on land.
explain: Nautical can also describe decorations. A nautical theme uses anchors, ropes and sailor-style stripes. Ask yourself: is this about the sea or ships? If yes, nautical is probably the right word.
fact: Nautical means to do with ships, sailing or sailors.
fact: A nautical mile is a unit of distance at sea, about 1.85 km.
fact: «Territorial waters» reach 12 nautical miles from the coast, so the nautical mile is used to measure the sea.
fact: A nautical chart is a map used for sailing at sea.
fact: Nautical stripes and a nautical theme are designs that copy ships and the sea.
exercise: «Countries also have borders at sea, with territorial waters reaching 12 nautical miles from the coast.» In this sentence, what is a nautical mile? | *A unit of distance at sea, about 1.85 km | A small land map | Ten metres on a playground | A unit of time for cooking
exercise: Mia's new top has nautical stripes. What does nautical describe here? | Snow and ice | Plants and flowers | *Sea and ship designs
exercise: A sailor reads a nautical chart before the trip. What is a nautical chart? | A picture book of birds | A recipe for fish pie | *A map for sailing at sea
test: A ship's crew learns nautical terms. What are nautical terms? | *Words used by sailors and at sea | Words for rain | Words about the moon | Words about cooking
test: Which of these is a nautical theme? | Cactus and sand | Snowmen and scarves | *Anchors and sailor-style stripes | Trains and tunnels
exam: A nautical mile is about how many kilometres? | About 100 m | *About 1.85 km | About 1 cm | About 10 km
